# nix-headscale-ha .gitignore

# ── Nix build artifacts ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
result
result-*

# ── Generated PKI (contains private keys — never commit unencrypted) ─────────
# The gen-test-secrets.sh script writes certs to ./pki/ by default.
# The ENCRYPTED form lives in tests/secrets.yaml and is safe to commit.
pki/
*.key
# (*.crt files are public material — you may choose to track them, but they
#  live inside the SOPS bundle too so there's no need)

# ── Unencrypted secrets draft (safe to commit only when SOPS-encrypted) ──────
# If you ran gen-test-secrets.sh with --no-encrypt, the result is plaintext:
# tests/secrets.yaml  ← comment this line out if you want to track the
#                        SOPS-encrypted version (recommended)

# ── Editor / OS artefacts ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
.direnv
